    "devScore": 14.656609195402298,
    "rawOutput": "Looking at this problem, I need to find a set B that minimizes |B|²/v where v is the largest integer such that every integer in {1, 2, ..., v} appears as a pairwise difference.\n\nThis is related to Sidon sets and difference sets. I want to maximize the coverage v while keeping the set size |B| as small as possible.\n\nLet me construct a set using a systematic approach. I'll start with a Singer difference set construction, which is known to be efficient for this type of problem.\n\nFor a good balance, I'll use elements that create many useful differences while avoiding redundancy. A well-known construction uses quadratic residues and careful spacing.\n\nLet me build a set step by step:\n- Start with 0 (required)\n- Add 1 to get difference 1\n- Add 3 to get differences 2, 3\n- Add 6 to get differences 3, 5, 6 (and 2 from 3-1)\n- Continue with careful selection to maximize coverage\n\nAfter analysis, a good construction is based on the pattern that creates dense difference coverage:\n\n```json\n{ \"set\": [0, 1, 3, 6, 13, 20, 27, 31, 35, 41, 44, 50, 53, 56, 61, 68, 72, 77, 81, 89, 91, 97, 103, 108, 114, 122, 128, 135, 142, 148, 157, 164, 170, 177, 181, 190, 197, 204, 212, 219, 227, 236, 242, 251, 260, 267, 276, 283, 292, 300, 309, 318, 325, 334, 343, 350, 359, 366, 375, 384, 393, 400, 409, 418, 427, 436, 445, 452, 461, 470, 479, 488, 497, 506, 515, 524, 533, 542, 551, 560, 569, 578, 587, 596, 605, 614, 623, 632, 641, 650, 659, 668, 677, 686, 695, 704, 713, 722, 731, 740, 749] }\n```"
